# This is a client-side-routed SPA (React Router) - every real page still
# needs to serve index.html so the JS can take over and render the right
# route. But a single blanket "/* /index.html 200" rule (the previous
# version of this file) meant ANY url, including typos, dead links, or bots
# probing random paths, rendered the app shell with an EMPTY <main> (no
# matching <Route>, nothing rendered) while still returning HTTP 200 - a
# real "screen with no publisher content" being served with ads, and served
# with a success status to crawlers on top of that.
#
# Fix: list every real route explicitly with 200, then fall back to 404 for
# everything else - index.html is still served either way (so the SPA's own
# NotFoundPage renders a real, helpful page for human visitors), but
# genuinely unknown paths now correctly report HTTP 404 instead of 200.
/                 /index.html   200
/history          /index.html   200
/contact          /index.html   200
/faq              /index.html   200
/terms            /index.html   200
/privacy          /index.html   200
/*                /index.html   404
